# ERP Frontend

- Preserve behavior; refactor incrementally. Do not remove features unless replaced.
- Workspace UI is ERP-dense: tables first, sticky toolbars/headers, right-side summaries, dialogs only for focused tasks.
- Use `DataTable` (`variant="erp"`) for list pages. Support sort, filter, sticky header, and row actions before inventing a new table.
- Posted documents (`COMPLETED`, `CANCELLED`, `VOIDED`) are read-only. Void/cancel instead of delete for money records.
- Show audit fields (`created_by`, timestamps, status) on document views.
- Keep hospitality labels that users know (`Bookings`, `Stays`) unless a real ERP document exists. Prefer `Customers`, `Employees`, `Financials`, `Inventory`.
- Do not duplicate tax/overtime math in the UI; use tenant rates from the API.
- Keyboard: Escape closes dialogs; row click opens the record. Icon-only buttons need `aria-label`.
- Change only the files required for the page being refactored.
